INT. CLOCKMAKER'S SHOP, BACK ROOM - NIGHT

Dozens of clocks ticking out of step. A vault door, ajar.

Four thieves crowd the doorway in dark clothes.

MARGOT "THE MOUSE" ILLINGWORTH-BASSEY (40s, crew leader) holds a stopwatch.

VICTOR OKONKWO-REYES (30s, safecracker) presses a stethoscope to the vault.

DELPHINE "DEL" ARMSTRONG-KATZ (20s, driver) shifts on her feet.

SOLOMON "SOL" QUILLFEATHER (50s, lookout, bowler hat) peers through the shutters.

MARGOT
(to the crew)
Ninety seconds. Everyone know their job?

SOL
I watch.

DEL
I drive.

VICTOR
I listen.

MARGOT
Good. Victor, tumblers.

VICTOR
(muttering)
Come on, you old beauty.

A click. Another. The door swings wide. Inside: velvet cases, empty.

MARGOT
Empty.

VICTOR
Empty?

DEL
Margot--

MARGOT
Quiet.

Every clock in the shop strikes midnight at once. A cacophony of chimes.

A figure steps out from between the grandfather clocks: ALISTAIR PEMBERTON-SHAW (60s, nightshirt, shotgun, mildly annoyed).

ALISTAIR
Evening. I moved it Tuesday.

The crew freezes. Sol removes his bowler hat.

SOL
Tuesday?

ALISTAIR
Tuesday.

MARGOT
(to herself)
Of course it was Tuesday.

Alistair lowers the shotgun, sighs.

ALISTAIR
There's tea. Stay for tea.
